{"reference":"Zechariah 5","book":"Zechariah","chapter":5,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Visions of wrongdoing removed","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter presents wrongdoing through two vivid visions. A flying scroll carries a curse against theft and false swearing that reaches into offenders’ homes. The second vision portrays Wickedness as a woman shut inside an ephah under a lead weight, then carried by winged women to a prepared house in Shinar. The imagery strongly depicts wrongdoing as both exposed and removed, though the precise meaning of its figures and destination remains debated.","verse_refs":["Zechariah 5:1-4","Zechariah 5:5-11"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_zechariah_005_8ffa7ea2c262425f1c0c80c1"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}